@page "/privacy-policy"
<PageTitle>Privacy Policy - The Singularity Workshop</PageTitle>

<div class="container py-5">
    <h1 class="display-4 fw-bold text-dark mb-4">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="lead text-muted">
        This policy governs the data practices of The Singularity Workshop regarding the
        <strong>TheSingularityWorkshop.com</strong> website and all related services, including the FSM API software asset.
    </p>

    <hr class="my-5" />

    <h2 class="h3 fw-bold text-success">Data Collection Policy:</h2>
    <h1>We do NOT collect any user data.</h1>
    <div class="card p-4 mb-4 border-success">
        <h3 class="h4 text-success mb-3">Your Privacy is Our Default State</h3>
        <p>
            <strong>The Singularity Workshop</strong> collects NO personal identifying information (PII) from users.
        </p>

        <h4 class="h5 mt-3 text-info">What this means: Zero Collection</h4>
        <ul>
            <li>
                <strong>Website:</strong> We do not use cookies, trackers, proprietary analytics, or any technology to monitor your browsing behavior on <strong>TheSingularityWorkshop.com</strong>.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>FSM API Software:</strong> The FSM API is a pure logic framework. It does <strong>NOT</strong> collect, transmit, or store any data from your application or runtime environment.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Third-Party Links:</strong> We may redirect you to external platforms (e.g., NuGet, CoderLegion, etc.). Any data collected by these third parties is governed solely by their respective privacy policies.
            </li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <hr class="mt-5" />

    <p class="text-muted small text-center">
        This policy ensures compliance while reflecting our core philosophy. For questions regarding our Zero Data Policy, please use the <a href="support">Support / Contact</a> page.
    </p>
</div>
